{"round":1,"event":"llm_response","agent_id":0,"input_tokens":1126,"output_tokens":189,"response":"A collaborative approach is required to compute $C = A \\times B$. Agent 0 will compute its portion of the result matrix $C$.\n\n**Agent 0 Computation:**\nAgent 0 has $A[0, :] = [4, 3]$ and the full $B = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 8 \\end{pmatrix}$.\nWe compute $C[0, j] = A[0, 0] \\times B[0, j] + A[0, 1] \\times B[1, j]$.\n\n$C[0, 0] = 4 \\times 2 + 3 \\times 8 = 8 + 24 = 32$\n$C[0, 1] = 4 \\times 3 + 3 \\times 8 = 12 + 24 = 36$\nSo, Agent 0 computes the first row of $C$: $[32, 36]$.\n\nAgent 0 needs Agent 1 to compute the remaining row $C[1, :]$, which depends on $A[1, :]$ (assumed held by Agent 1) and $B$. Agent 0 will wait for Agent 1's contribution before submitting the final result.\n\n<tool_call>\n  <tool>wait</tool>\n  <parameters>\n  </parameters>\n</tool_call>","timestamp":"2026-10-19T13:39:57.066409+00:00"}
